IMPORT `euca-nouns`
IMPORT `euca-shared`

-- Section 205: definitions. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- "For purposes of this title" the Act defines eleven terms. Where a definition classifies a
-- payment or a place, it is a rule over facts a witness could state. Where it hands the meaning to
-- the applicable State law (benefit year, base period, week) or to an office (the Secretary, the
-- State agency, State law), the State's or the office's answer is a plain input, and the rule
-- says only that the Act takes that answer.
-- These rules decide nothing about who owes whom what; section 205 has no right, duty, power or
-- immunity in it (NOTES.md, Jural relations: none).
-- out of text: the applicable State law's definitions of benefit year, base period and week;
-- 5 U.S.C. chapter 85; section 3304 of the Internal Revenue Code (approval of State laws).

§ `Section 205: definitions`

§§ `205(1) to (4): kinds of compensation`

-- src:120 | “(1) The term ‘compensation’ means cash benefits payable to individuals with respect to their unemployment.
@ref s 205(1) (src:120)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment to an individual`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the payment is compensation` payment MEANS
        payment's `cash benefits`
    AND payment's `payable with respect to the individual's unemployment`

-- src:123 | “(4) The term ‘additional compensation’ means compensation payable to exhaustees by reason of conditions of high unemployment or by reason of other special factors.
@ref s 205(4) (src:123)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment to an individual`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the payment is additional compensation` payment MEANS
        `the payment is compensation` payment
    AND payment's `payable to exhaustees by reason of conditions of high unemployment or by reason of other special factors`

-- src:122 | “(3) The term ‘extended compensation’ means compensation (including additional compensation and compensation payable pursuant to 5 U.S.C. chapter 85) payable for weeks of unemployment beginning in an extended benefit period to an individual under those provisions of the State law which satisfy the requirements of this title with respect to the payment of extended compensation.
@ref s 205(3) (src:122)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment to an individual`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the payment is extended compensation` payment MEANS
        `the payment is compensation` payment
    AND (   payment's `payable under a State unemployment compensation law`
         OR payment's `payable pursuant to 5 U.S.C. chapter 85`)
    AND payment's `for a week of unemployment beginning in an extended benefit period`
    AND payment's `under provisions of the State law which satisfy the requirements of this title with respect to the payment of extended compensation`

-- src:121 | “(2) The term ‘regular compensation’ means compensation payable to an individual under any State unemployment compensation law (including compensation payable pursuant to 5 U.S.C. chapter 85), other than extended compensation and additional compensation.
@ref s 205(2) (src:121)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment to an individual`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the payment is regular compensation` payment MEANS
        `the payment is compensation` payment
    AND (   payment's `payable under a State unemployment compensation law`
         OR payment's `payable pursuant to 5 U.S.C. chapter 85`)
    AND (NOT `the payment is extended compensation` payment)
    AND (NOT `the payment is additional compensation` payment)

§§ `205(5), (6), (11): as the applicable State law defines`

-- src:124 | “(5) The term ‘benefit year’ means the benefit year as defined in the applicable State law.
@ref s 205(5) (src:124)
GIVEN `first day of the benefit year under the applicable State law` IS A DATE
      `last day of the benefit year under the applicable State law` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Benefit year`
`the benefit year under section 205(5)` `first day of the benefit year under the applicable State law` `last day of the benefit year under the applicable State law` MEANS
    `Benefit year` WITH
        `first day of the benefit year` IS `first day of the benefit year under the applicable State law`
        `last day of the benefit year` IS `last day of the benefit year under the applicable State law`

-- src:125 | “(6) The term ‘base period’ means the base period as determined under applicable State law for the benefit year.
@ref s 205(6) (src:125)
GIVEN `first day of the base period under the applicable State law` IS A DATE
      `last day of the base period under the applicable State law` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Base period`
`the base period under section 205(6)` `first day of the base period under the applicable State law` `last day of the base period under the applicable State law` MEANS
    `Base period` WITH
        `first day of the base period` IS `first day of the base period under the applicable State law`
        `last day of the base period` IS `last day of the base period under the applicable State law`

-- src:130 | “(11) The term ‘week’ means a week as defined in the applicable State law.
@ref s 205(11) (src:130)
GIVEN `day on which the week begins under the applicable State law` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the week under section 205(11)` `day on which the week begins under the applicable State law` MEANS
    `day on which the week begins under the applicable State law`

§§ `205(7), (9), (10): the Secretary, the State agency and State law`

-- src:126 | “(7) The term ‘Secretary’ means the Secretary of Labor of the United States.
@ref s 205(7) (src:126)
GIVETH A Party
`the Secretary under section 205(7)` MEANS `the Secretary of Labor`

-- src:128 | “(9) The term ‘State agency’ means the agency of the State which administers its State law.
@ref s 205(9) (src:128)
GIVEN `the agency administers the State law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the agency is the State agency` `the agency administers the State law` MEANS
    `the agency administers the State law`

-- src:129 | “(10) The term ‘State law’ means the unemployment compensation law of the State, approved by the Secretary under section 3304 of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986.
@ref s 205(10) (src:129)
GIVEN `it is the unemployment compensation law of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has approved it under section 3304 of the Internal Revenue Code` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the law is the State law` `it is the unemployment compensation law of the State` `the Secretary has approved it under section 3304 of the Internal Revenue Code` MEANS
        `it is the unemployment compensation law of the State`
    AND `the Secretary has approved it under section 3304 of the Internal Revenue Code`

§§ `205(8): State`

-- src:127 | “(8) The term ‘State’ includes the District of Columbia, the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico, and the Virgin Islands.
@ref s 205(8) (src:127)
GIVEN place IS A Place
GIVETH A `Status of a place under the definition of State`
`the status of the place under the definition of State` place MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `a State of the United States` THEN `counts as a State for this title`
    WHEN `the District of Columbia` THEN `counts as a State for this title`
    WHEN `the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico` THEN `counts as a State for this title`
    WHEN `the Virgin Islands` THEN `counts as a State for this title`
    OTHERWISE `is not named by the definition of State, which says only what a State includes`
